#: ../../source/integrations-guide/run-slash-commands.rst:7
msgid ""
"Using a slash command is as easy as composing a message. Instead of "
"message text, you start slash commands with a slash character: ``/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/run-slash-commands.rst:9
msgid ""
"For example, if you want to log out of Mattermost using only your "
"keyboard, you can enter ``/logout`` in the message text box and select "
"**Send**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/run-slash-commands.rst:11
msgid ""
"Because your message starts with a slash ``/``, Mattermost knows it's a "
"slash command, and performs the action defined for that command."
msgstr ""

